1. Microservices Development
The monolithic Coffee Suppliers application was divided into two independent microservices:
- Customer Microservice – provides supplier information to customers.
- Employee Microservice – provides administrative functionality for managing suppliers.
2. Docker Containerization
Separate Docker images were created for both microservices.
Customer Application → Docker Image → Amazon ECR
Employee Application → Docker Image → Amazon ECR

The images were pushed to Amazon ECR and later used by ECS.
3. Amazon ECS Deployment
An ECS cluster named:
microservices-serverlesscluster

was created using AWS Fargate.
Two ECS services were deployed:
customer-microservice
employee-microservice

Both services use container port 8080.
4. Application Load Balancer
An Application Load Balancer named:
microservicesLB

was configured to route requests between the two microservices.
/              → Customer Microservice
/admin/*       → Employee Microservice

The /admin/* route was also restricted using a source-IP rule.
5. Amazon RDS Integration
The microservices were connected to an Amazon RDS MySQL database containing the coffee supplier information.
The Customer service displays supplier information, while the Employee service provides administrative operations.
6. AWS CodeCommit
The application source code was maintained in AWS CodeCommit repositories:
microservices
deployment

The dev branch was used for the implementation.
7. AWS CodePipeline
Two automated CI/CD pipelines were created:
update-customer-microservice
update-employee-microservice

The pipeline automatically processes the application source and container image before deployment.
8. AWS CodeDeploy
AWS CodeDeploy was configured for ECS Blue/Green deployment.
Deployment groups:
microservices-customer
microservices-employee

AppSpec files were used to specify the ECS service, container name, and container port.
9. Service Scaling
The Customer microservice was scaled to three desired tasks:
Desired tasks: 3
Running tasks: 3
Healthy tasks: 3
Unhealthy tasks: 0

10. Final Verification
The implementation was verified by accessing:
Customer:
http://<ALB-DNS>/suppliers

Employee:
http://<ALB-DNS>/admin/suppliers

The Customer page successfully displayed supplier information, and the Employee page provided the administrative supplier interface.
Both CI/CD pipelines completed successfully, and the ECS services were running successfully.
